      "writtenOn": "2023-12-14T16:16:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"Topic e-ac3-joc remote submix removed\" so that merge of this CL isn\u0027t blocked unnecessarily by other CLs.",
      "revId": "ce9767a966c9c921e7507985d32ae60e8c6007e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0538c03b_00610b41",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/default/r_submix/ModuleRemoteSubmix.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-22T00:09:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Dean, I realized this does not look right to me. You are declaring direct ports for PCM. But here you are checking that the format is non-PCM.\n\n```\n//  * \"r_submix output direct\", DIRECT|IEC958_NONAUDIO, 1 max open, 1 max active\n//    - profile PCM 16-bit; STEREO; 8000, 11025, 16000, 32000, 44100, 48000, 192000\n//  * \"r_submix input direct\", DIRECT, 1 max open, 1 max active\n//    - profile PCM 16-bit; STEREO; 8000, 11025, 16000, 32000, 44100, 48000, 192000\n```\n\nIn fact, what I\u0027m seeing while running `atest audiorouting_tests` is that the system first opens a remote submix output for \"8 kHz, DIRECT|IEC\", and this succeeds. And then, the framework also opens the same remote submix output for \"192 kHz\" without flags. This seems like a wrong behavior to me.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "ce9767a966c9c921e7507985d32ae60e8c6007e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c525b37d_7c4f96f1",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/default/r_submix/ModuleRemoteSubmix.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1133568
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-22T02:16:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The design relies upon AudioFlinger IEC61937 encapsulation of compressed audio data, as well as the AudioMix registered with the raw compressed audio format.\n\nThis results in AudioPolicy requests to AudioFlinger to open inputs/outputs in the raw compressed format first; it is required that these raw compressed format (e.g. e-ac-3-joc) fail in the remote submix HAL. When this failure is returned to AudioFlinger, AF will attempt to reopen the stream on the HAL in PCM format, but will wrap the compressed audio data in IEC61937 frames. This is why we are checking here if the format type is PCM and if not failing.\n\nDoes that help explain the expectations?",
      "parentUuid": "0538c03b_00610b41",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "ce9767a966c9c921e7507985d32ae60e8c6007e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "02d5ea04_8289e7e2",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/default/r_submix/ModuleRemoteSubmix.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1133568
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-22T02:21:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the above, the sentence \"This is why we are checking here if the format type is PCM and if not failing.\" should read \"This is why we are checking here the format type and failing if it\u0027s not PCM\".",
      "parentUuid": "c525b37d_7c4f96f1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "ce9767a966c9c921e7507985d32ae60e8c6007e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4d2c6b7e_bdc19d1f",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/default/r_submix/ModuleRemoteSubmix.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-22T04:53:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e This results in AudioPolicy requests to AudioFlinger to open inputs/outputs in the raw compressed format first\n\nThat is what seems contradictory to me. Since the direct profiles are declared as \u0027PCM\u0027, not as encoded formats, why would APM open them for encoded formats? I know, it can, but that looks like an issue with the APM. It seems to be largely ignoring the declared capabilities of mix ports specifically for remote submix. For example, the canonical remote submix config file only lists 48 kHz sampling rate, however APM can effectively open it an any other rate, which looks like a wrong behavior to me. But if we consider an \"ideal\" APM behavior, I don\u0027t see why would it attempt to try opening ports using the format that they do not declare.",
      "parentUuid": "02d5ea04_8289e7e2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "ce9767a966c9c921e7507985d32ae60e8c6007e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7f9b53fb_c6053a8d",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/default/r_submix/ModuleRemoteSubmix.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1133568
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-22T10:42:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is the current behaviour of AudioPolicyManager::registerPolicyMixes which calls rSubmixModule-\u003eaddOutputProfile and rSubmixModule-\u003eaddInputProfile for loopback mixes, and those requests aren\u0027t filtered by the r submix mixports that have been read in as part of APM initialization (AudioPolicyInterface* createAudioPolicyManager).\n\nI conceptually thought of this as a different \"dynamic mixPort\" mechanism; the other dynamic feature in APM is for the HDMI output case where EDID capabilities are dynamic and they also update APM with additional mixPort capabilities beyond what is declared in the audio policy config file. In either case, the capabilities of the HAL as seen by APM can be more than the config file declared caps. The main difference between dynamic mix port and this dynamic audio policy is the former dynamic capability is based on the HAL reporting it to the framework/APM, whereas in the latter it is a system app (e.g. phone projection transmitter) which is determining this dynamic capability (of the phone projection receiver) and using AudioPolicy registerMix to add this.\n\nIn both cases, the current design and implementation seems OK to me.",
      "parentUuid": "4d2c6b7e_bdc19d1f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "ce9767a966c9c921e7507985d32ae60e8c6007e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "080fc0d7_7f4e5867",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/default/r_submix/ModuleRemoteSubmix.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-03T00:35:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, all these theoretical considerations are fine, but they are not helping. While I was landing the topic to switch Cuttlefish to AIDL, I have temporarily reverted this CL because it was seemingly causing issues with `audiorouting_tests` and `audiosystem_tests`. And now I\u0027m re-applying it, having added these tests to presubmit for the HAL code, and these tests are failing again in the presubmit: https://r.android.com/c/platform/hardware/interfaces/+/2893424/1?tab\u003dchecks. This proves that something is wrong with the assumption that this change is \"OK\". What I\u0027m seeing is that the framework first opens the presubmit output with \"direct\" flags for PCM format, and then opens it again, this time without \"direct\" flags, and without previously closing the \"direct\" stream. If you have time, PTAL because I have a backlog of issues that I need to take a look at. Sorry for the trouble.",
      "parentUuid": "7f9b53fb_c6053a8d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "ce9767a966c9c921e7507985d32ae60e8c6007e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
